The storage layer will live in codegen, not parser: I’ll add a `sqlite` mode and `createSQLiteWorkspaceIndex()`, backed by `.oa-cache/state.sqlite` by default. The implementation will treat SQLite as an optimization cache: schema or option mismatches clear stale rows and force the next diff to a full rebuild; DB open/write/read failures drop into full-rebuild fallback instead of breaking correctness.
I’m adding the SQLite-backed implementation now. The main edit is a new codegen storage file plus small public factory/type exports from the existing workspace-index boundary.
I’m extending the existing workspace-index test suite with the storage-specific cases from the acceptance criteria: schema/meta creation, schema/compatibility rebuild, rollback on failed writes, and full-rebuild fallback when SQLite cannot open.
